1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,963
A Moon base may breathe 30% oxygen at 10.2 psi. Does NASA’s fire data cover it?

2
00:00:03,013 --> 00:00:05,799
EMBER ranks 20 NASA investigations against your habitat and says what each one covers

3
00:00:05,849 --> 00:00:09,358
Key finding: no solid-material test in NASA’s PSI data goes above 22.2% oxygen

4
00:00:09,408 --> 00:00:13,064
Six findings computed from NASA’s own rows: on the ground, Saffire-II samples burned further than in orbit

5
00:00:13,114 --> 00:00:15,690
Every number is one click from the cells NASA wrote

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:19,725
We read every cell of NASA’s 21 tables and documented 37 data-quality issues

7
00:00:19,775 --> 00:00:24,309
Gemini writes the analysis; EMBER checks every quote and number against its source

8
00:00:24,359 --> 00:00:27,554
It shows what the research informs: detection, suppression, ventilation

9
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:29,974
Open NASA data, measured findings, checked AI, honest limits
